// core - foundational Frust pod: not "add-ons," the basics every other
// pod in this library builds on.
//
// This file is required to exist (frate's convention for a lib pod's
// entry point), but its own content is intentionally just this comment -
// the actual functions live in the other files under src/, compiled
// together with this one as a single unit via frust_compiler's multi-file
// support:
//
//   console_io.fr  - string formatting/concatenation, println_*
//   math.fr        - abs/min/max/clamp, trig, libm extras (pow/log/floor/...)
//   string.fr      - libc string.h (only the 64-bit-safe parts - see file)
//   mem.fr         - malloc/free/realloc/memcpy/memset/memmove
//   file_io.fr     - fopen/fread/fwrite/fgets (no fclose yet - see file)
//   time.fr        - clock() only (see file for why time() isn't here)
//
// string.fr/mem.fr/file_io.fr all document the same real gap: Frust has
// no i32 type, so any libc function returning a plain C `int` can't be
// wrapped safely yet (strcmp, fclose, feof, ...). Not silently missing -
// each file lists exactly what's blocked and why.
